[
    {
        "content": "<p>While reviewing a PR I wrote that after a multiline statement the proof needs to go on a separate line. So that for example the following code</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isOpen_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompactlyCoherentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsOpen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsCompact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsOpen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↓∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsCoherentWith</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isOpen_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCoherentWith</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>should be formatted like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isOpen_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CompactlyCoherentSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsOpen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsCompact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsOpen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↓∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IsCoherentWith</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isOpen_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isCoherentWith</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I noticed afterwards that the first option is not explicitly against the style guide. I think this case is somewhat implied by the guide but not mentioned explicitly. Is there clear consensus on whether the first option is accepted? Should this be mentioned more clearly in the guide?</p>",
        "id": 583216794,
        "sender_full_name": "Hannah Scholz",
        "timestamp": 1775120943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think there is consensus on this. I believe that quite a few very active mathlib contributors often use the first style if the line length linter permits it.</p>",
        "id": 583217429,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1775121128
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also think that there is no consensus and probably depends on how complicated the proof is.  I prefer the multiline approach.  I would probably be happy to accept a <code>rfl</code> proof on the same line.</p>",
        "id": 583217691,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1775121198
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that putting the proof on the same line is fine iff it is very short (e.g. <code>rfl</code>, perhaps <code>by simp</code>). The above proof is way too long for that --- putting it on the <del>same</del> next line is more readable.</p>",
        "id": 583218076,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Rothgang",
        "timestamp": 1775121314
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree with Michael, modulo the negation of the statement after <code>---</code>, which I think is the intended message anyway.</p>",
        "id": 583218371,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1775121414
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, edited.</p>",
        "id": 583234010,
